Henry doesn't hang out there, either.  I personally still have yet to
hear anything that can be gained from this that isn't more easily or
effectively gained elsewhere; I agree with the other posters who
question whether the term "abuse" is being used correctly in this instance.

For example, I can dig out an entire level, cover it with pits, and then
put on a ring of levitation and freely move around while other creatures
fall in and are trapped.  Does this do what it says on the tin?  Yes.
Is it, say, "pickaxe abuse", though?  Hardly.

> Cloning web spaces using #untrap sounds like a bug more than anything
> else.  What's the message the game gives for this?

It's a feature.  If you #untrap your pet while it's in a web, you get
warned 'Whoops, the web sticks to you too!', and then the web appears on
your square as well -- but you are stuck in the web.

Wielding Sting, you can cut through the web and then #untrap your pet
again, thus letting you create 8 additional web squares from the first.
 To continue with this, you'll have to arrange to get your pet stuck
again (requires magic whistle, of course) in a square that has a
reasonable amount of empty spaces nearby; ideally a corner so you can
web the next 5.  With a sufficient amount of effort you could
theoretically web the entire level... to what purpose, well, that's
another story entirely.

